 A labeled expression consumes the longest
 `argument_expression` as its payload. Nesting requires parens: `x: (y: 1)`.
+
+Nyad children accept the same expressions as list elements, including labels and blocks.
+Nyads still have at most two children.
+
+A binding form contains a header of named clauses followed by one body block.
+An inspection header contains the subject and two binder names.
+Its three blocks are the leaf, stem, and fork clauses, in that order.
 
