+The brackets in `@[...]` contain a literal list of tag entries. Each entry can
+be any expression. A list-valued entry remains one entry rather than being flattened.
+Consecutive annotation headers concatenate their entry lists in source order.
+
 The main feature of tagging is that it doesn't affect the application
 of terms. The following guarantees hold:
+
+Here, `v` is an untagged payload, and `m` and `n` are arbitrary tag entries.
+
 ```
 @[m] v      == ~[[m], v]
+@[m, n] v   == ~[[m, n], v]
 @[m] @[n] v == ~[[m, n], v]
+@[] v       == ~[[], v]
 @(@[m] v)   => [[m], v]
 (@[m] v)(x) => v(x)
